{
  "name": "cleansweep",
  "display_name": "CleanSweep (floor robot + suction climber)",
  "task": "A vacuum-mop floor robot cleans the floors and lifts a small suction climber onto counters and glass to wipe them, then empties itself at its dock.",
  "trigger": {
    "type": "phone_button",
    "label": "Clean the kitchen",
    "options": [
      "Route: react to the mess / scripted demo",
      "Surfaces: floors + counters + glass / floors only"
    ],
    "notify_on": [
      "done",
      "blocked",
      "needs_help"
    ]
  },
  "form_factor": "wheeled",
  "footprint_m": [
    0.4,
    0.42
  ],
  "height_m": 0.32,
  "reach_m": 0.42,
  "payload_kg": 1.0,
  "speed_mps": 0.3,
  "battery_h": 2.5,
  "bom_usd": 2200,
  "bom_assumptions": "Quantity-1 component prices, 2026. Floor robot base = lidar, vacuum fan + brush roll, mop module with 2 tanks, 2 drive motors, 5 Ah battery, bumper. Dock station = pumps, tanks, dust-bag fan, pad heater. Climber = 4 suction chambers with one 12 V fan, 2 tread motors, 1 Ah battery, microfibre pad, spray pump. Compute = Jetson Orin Nano (~$250) + RGB-D camera (~$150). The robot runs at 0.3 m/s in the sim (below the 0.6-1.0 wheeled range) because it is cleaning while it drives.",
  "cost_drivers": [
    [
      "Floor robot base: lidar, vacuum, mop module, battery, motors",
      650
    ],
    [
      "Telescoping mast + lift cradle + crevice arm",
      450
    ],
    [
      "Suction climber: 4-chamber fan, treads, battery, spray pad",
      420
    ]
  ],
  "env_changes_required": [
    "Dock at the dead end of the hallway needs a wall outlet (~$150 if one isn't there).",
    "Push dining chairs in when the robot runs: the 0.45 m gap between them is only 5 cm wider than the robot.",
    "Keep a ~25 cm strip on counters clear where the climber is launched (here: the west end of the island).",
    "Cords, socks and pet toys off the floor before a run (the robot avoids them but skips that area)."
  ],
  "tasks_excluded": [
    "Painted drywall walls: suction on matte, porous paint is unreliable and a failed grip drops the climber; only glass, tile, stone and cabinet fronts.",
    "Wall-to-ceiling corners and above 1.9 m: past the mast's reach, and the climber never transitions between surfaces on its own.",
    "Cleaning around the stove, sink and knives: those are keep-out zones; the climber cleans the rest of the counter.",
    "Moving objects off counters: it cleans around them and reports what it skipped.",
    "Scheduled runs (daily floors, weekly glass): team rule is on-demand only, but the button works remotely from the app.",
    "Pet messes: detected and avoided, never spread; it notifies the user."
  ],
